# Testing Policy — Manual Testing Only

1. Do NOT create, generate, modify, or execute any test cases unless the user explicitly requests it.
2. Do NOT automatically create unit, integration, or E2E tests; test files/classes/mocks/fixtures; or test plans/scenarios.
3. Do NOT run `dotnet test`, `npm test`, `ng test`, or any other test command unless explicitly instructed.
4. The user is responsible for manually testing all changes. Do not treat testing as part of implementation tasks.
5. Focus only on implementing the requested functionality. Avoid unnecessary code, refactoring, files, or features outside scope.
6. Build/compilation checks are allowed when needed to catch compile errors. Do not run automated tests.
7. After a task, summarize: changes made, files modified, and brief considerations for manual testing. Do not generate test cases or detailed testing instructions unless requested.
8. Do not override this policy unless the user explicitly authorizes testing.
